# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement data. NEVER commit these.
#
# net_monitor.db holds the `net` table, which records the gateway MAC address,
# the wifi SSID and the subnet of every network this has run on. A router's MAC
# is a wifi-geolocation key (WiGLE, Google, Apple all index them), so publishing
# one pins the machine to a physical address. The logs and eval artefacts carry
# the same identifiers in plain text.
#
# Anyone cloning this repo gets an empty database on first run, which is the
# correct starting state anyway - baselines are per-network and do not transfer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net_monitor.db
net_monitor.db-shm
net_monitor.db-wal
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

net_alerts.log
net_history.jsonl
net_eval_results*.json
net_eval_stopping.json
# Per-scenario runs (net_eval.py --save). Eval artefacts hold the agent's full answers, which
# quote the SSID, the gateway address and this machine's local IPs - the same identifiers the
# database is kept out of the repo for. net_eval_results*.json alone did not match a --save
# under any other name.
eval_*.json
# The rendered report. It quotes the SSID, the gateway and this machine's addresses by
# design - that is what makes it useful and what keeps it out of the repo.
net_report.html

# Local configuration: may name internal hosts. monitor.example.json is tracked.
monitor.json
monitor.json.bak.*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party papers. Publisher PDFs (Elsevier, ACM, IEEE) are licensed for
# personal use, not redistribution. REFERENCES.md lists them by DOI instead.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
papers/
*.pdf

# Vendored browser tooling, not part of this project
check_datat_base_tool/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env

# Database backups. *.db alone missed net_monitor.db.bak-<stamp>, and git add -A would have
# published the gateway MAC and SSID inside it. Anything that starts with the database name
# or carries a backup suffix stays local.
net_monitor.db*
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.bak.*
